fastent release notes
=====================

This file contains user-visible changes for each release.  For a
complete source-level history, see the ChangeLog.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.0 (May 2026)

  * Initial release of fastent.

  * Banked 4-way SIMD histogram in the inner loop.

  * Serial correlation cross-product computed via widened signed
    multiply + horizontal add (PMADDUBSW-style on SSE/AVX2; the same
    algorithm widened to 64-byte vectors on AVX-512), with a
    sign-correction term derived on the fly from the byte sum.  No
    scalar fallback per byte.

  * Bit-mode (-b) population count: VPOPCNTB on AVX-512
    VPOPCNTDQ + BITALG hosts; PSHUFB nibble-LUT on AVX2 / SSE /
    SSSE3; __builtin_popcount in the scalar fallback.

  * Fused case-fold (-f) path: each loaded vector is folded
    in-register before the histogram, SCC, and Monte Carlo Pi
    kernels consume it -- no staging-copy prepass over the input,
    so -f keeps full SIMD throughput.

  * Runtime CPU dispatch: one binary picks the highest available
    variant among scalar / SSSE3 / SSE4.1 / AVX2 / AVX-512 (F + BW +
    CD + DQ + VL + VPOPCNTDQ + BITALG) at startup via
    __builtin_cpu_supports.  SIMD variants live in per-file static
    convenience libraries with isolated -m... CFLAGS so the rest of
    the binary stays at the configured baseline.

  * Fast I/O: mmap(2) with MADV_SEQUENTIAL / POSIX_FADV_SEQUENTIAL
    for regular files; a 2 MiB read(2) loop for stdin and unmappable
    sources.  --no-mmap forces the read(2) path.

  * Optional pthread worker pool (-j N / --threads N) partitioning
    the mmap region into 6-aligned slabs so the Monte-Carlo Pi state
    machine never crosses threads; merge order is deterministic and
    yields byte-identical output to the single-threaded run.

  * Outputs: human-readable, CSV (-t), or JSON (--json).  Adds a
    -p / --full-precision flag that renders every float at %.17g.

  * Test + bench harness: `make check` runs a deterministic-fixture
    sanity suite (fixtures live in $(builddir)/tests/fixtures so the
    source tree stays read-only-clean); `make bench` sweeps 10
    deterministic datasets through three modes and a power-of-two
    -j ladder, with ent(1) timed alongside if it is on PATH.

  * Build system: GNU autotools (configure.ac / Makefile.am) with
    SSSE3 / SSE4.2 / AVX2 / AVX-512 intrinsic probes and per-variant
    CFLAGS isolation.  ./bootstrap regenerates autotools artefacts;
    ./configure --enable-native --enable-lto enables host-specific
    tuning and link-time optimisation.
